#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_l10n_mx_edi_approval_account
msgid ""
"\n"
"Account Approvals - Mexican EDI\n"
"===============================\n"
"\n"
"Splits the approval requests that create a journal entry by whether their\n"
"journal issues a CFDI (``account.journal.l10n_mx_edi_enabled``): a \"Fiscal\"\n"
"and a \"Non-Fiscal\" filter on the request search view, so the person who\n"
"invoices from approvals can work one pile at a time.\n"
"\n"
"Links each fiscal approval request to the SAT CFDI XML that backs it:\n"
"\n"
"- The invoice photo or PDF attached to the request (usually by the Telegram\n"
"  bot) is read through the extraction cascade — the SAT QR code first, then\n"
"  the stamped XML if one was attached, then OCR text, then the generative\n"
"  readers — into the ``l10n_mx_edi_ocr_*`` fields.\n"
"- The request is matched against the CFDI documents that the SAT mass\n"
"  download files in Documents (``document.document``): by UUID when one was\n"
"  read, otherwise by issuer RFC + total (±$1.00) + emission date (±3 days).\n"
"  One candidate links; zero or several send the request to manual review\n"
"  with the candidate list saved on it.\n"
"- The link is always recorded by UUID (the XML is the source of truth), a\n"
"  CFDI can back at most one request (unique index), and any difference\n"
"  between what was read and what the XML declares is kept as a discrepancy\n"
"  note. New XMLs arriving later re-run the matching for waiting requests.\n"
msgstr ""

