#. module: base
#: model_terms:ir.actions.act_window,help:base.ir_job_channel_act
msgid ""
"A channel bounds how many background jobs of its kind run\n"
"            concurrently across all job workers. Jobs whose channel is not\n"
"            listed here run with a capacity of 1. Archiving a channel pauses\n"
"            it: none of its jobs is claimed until it is restored."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:base.field_res_users_login_cooldown__source
msgid ""
"A client's address, an account (`account:<user id>`), or a login no account "
"carries (`login:<sha256 of the login>`)."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_l10n_mx_edi_account_collection
msgid ""
"A collection recorded by a collector carries the SAT form of payment of what"
" the customer handed over (01 cash, 02 check, 03 transfer, 04 card) instead "
"of falling back to transfer, so its payment complement declares the real "
"form of payment on the date the customer paid. A daily run stamps the "
"complements of collections whose invoices are stamped, while the money may "
"still be in the collector's custody, and warns the collection supervisor two"
" days before the SAT deadline (the 5th of the following month) of any still "
"unsent."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_account_collection_sale
msgid ""
"A collector collects a confirmed cash sale (immediate payment terms) where "
"it happens: the order is invoiced, dated the day the customer paid and "
"posted in one step, the invoice is issued (stamped, where a localization "
"issues invoices), and the payment is recorded in the collector's custody "
"with its receipt. A per-company switch, off by default, holds the sales "
"orders on credit terms of a salesperson who keeps collections past their "
"hand-in date."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_account_collection
msgid ""
"A collector records the customer's payment on the day the customer paid, in "
"a custody journal: the invoice is settled at once while the money stays "
"booked to the collector's custody account. The collector hands the money in "
"through a remittance, cash to a till or a bank deposit, which the treasury "
"validates; shortages are charged to the collector. A daily check reminds "
"collectors of custody held beyond its working days. The customer receives "
"the receipt by email with a link to verify it and to report a problem to the"
" collection supervisor."
msgstr ""

