#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_mail_telegram
msgid ""
"A user who connected Telegram (Preferences) receives their inbox "
"notifications, direct and group chats and channel mentions in Telegram, each"
" with a link back to Odoo and a Mark as Read button, according to "
"preferences that say always, only while away, or never. Nothing already read"
" in Odoo is sent: delivery waits a grace period and checks again. Replying "
"to one of those messages in Telegram posts the reply on the same record or "
"conversation as that user, under their access rights; a reply to an internal"
" note stays a note, and a reply that would reach external followers asks "
"first. They go to one chat: the one the user connected last through a bot "
"delivering them, or the one they choose in Preferences, which also says "
"whether they are being delivered and why not. When Telegram starts refusing "
"them, or the user blocks the bot, Odoo tells the user once, in Odoo. "
"Requires a bot with Deliver Odoo Notifications enabled; Connect Telegram "
"opens that bot. A Telegram group, connected with a link made in Odoo, is a "
"Telegram channel of Discuss: its people's messages are posted there as their"
" contacts, forum topics are sub-channels, and what Odoo users write goes to "
"the group under their names."
msgstr ""

