#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_base
msgid ""
"Define the base business and system models used by the server, including "
"users, companies, contacts, modules and access configuration. Loaded as the "
"foundation for application modules."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,summary:base.module_purchase_agreement
msgid "Define vendor agreements with prices and quantity or value commitments"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:base.module_form
msgid "Defined Reports"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_appointment_sms
msgid ""
"Defines a calendar SMS alarm marked as a default for new appointment types "
"and adds a phone-use notice to the booking form when SMS reminders are "
"selected. Sending uses the Calendar SMS dependency and requires a usable "
"recipient phone number and configured SMS service."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_partner_group_restricted
msgid ""
"Defines a restricted contact-editing group, a base field allowlist and "
"field-write enforcement with matching readonly view behavior. Consuming "
"addons extend the allowlist and supply any business-specific partner scope. "
"Read permissions continue to depend on the applicable framework access "
"rules; this addon does not grant unrestricted visibility to every contact."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_trade_agreement
msgid ""
"Defines abstract agreement and agreement-line behavior, validity dates, "
"price breaks and order integration. Supplies lifecycle checks and helpers "
"for applying agreement terms and tracking confirmed quantities. Sales and "
"purchase agreement addons provide the concrete business models and "
"interfaces."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_mixin_attribute
msgid ""
"Defines abstract models for entity-attribute-value families, including value"
" membership and usage checks. Consuming addons declare concrete attribute, "
"value and line models and link them to business records. This infrastructure"
" addon does not provide a standalone attribute-management application."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_trade_tender
msgid ""
"Defines abstract tender and tender-line records with offer quantities, "
"deadlines and award handling, plus invitation and rival-offer wizards. "
"Consuming sales and purchase addons define the direction and concrete order "
"models. Awards use recorded offers and selected quantities; this "
"infrastructure does not collect bids from external marketplaces."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_resource_asset
msgid ""
"Defines asset kinds and identifiers, hierarchical components, custody and "
"operator assignments, meter readings and service states. Specialized addons "
"add accounting, stock tracking and domain-specific asset types."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_marketing_automation
msgid ""
"Defines campaigns, participants and activity workflows with email and "
"server-action steps. Tracks execution, opens, clicks and replies and "
"provides a test-participant launch flow."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_sale_commission
msgid ""
"Defines commission plans, achievement rules, targets, forecasts and "
"reporting. Calculations use eligible sales and invoice data and the plan "
"dates and rates."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_spreadsheet_dashboard
msgid ""
"Defines dashboard groups, company and user-group access, favorites and "
"published spreadsheet content. Provides shared dashboard links and export "
"routes."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_loyalty
msgid ""
"Defines program rules, rewards, points and coupon cards with validity "
"conditions. Sales-channel addons apply these programs to their orders."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_team
msgid ""
"Defines shared team and membership records with company links, favorites and"
" application-specific usage hooks. Adds user team helpers and alias support "
"for adopting applications. Individual business addons select their team "
"usages and link their documents; installation alone does not enable every "
"listed application workflow."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_tax
msgid ""
"Defines tax records, groups, repartition data and fiscal-position tax "
"mappings used by order calculations. Adds product tax defaults and company "
"tax settings. Accounting-specific journal accounts and posting behavior are "
"supplied by the accounting addon."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_phone_call
msgid ""
"Defines the phone call every telephony source files on: the softphone, a "
"phone system and a company handset. Holds the number, direction, outcome, "
"timing, contact, responsible user and company, matches the number to a "
"contact of that company, and files the call's recordings on its timeline for"
" transcription. Placing, receiving and recording calls belong to the addons "
"that drive a line."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_timer
msgid ""
"Defines timer records, reusable model mixins and interface components for "
"elapsed-time tracking. Application models must adopt the mixins and connect "
"timer actions to their workflow; this addon supplies the shared timer "
"infrastructure."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_hr_work_entry
msgid ""
"Defines work-entry types, durations and validation states. Generates entries"
" from employee schedules, identifies conflicts and provides regeneration for"
" selected employees and dates."
msgstr ""

