#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_integration_google
msgid ""
"Keeps each company's Google OAuth client in the credential vault and calls "
"Google APIs through the integration transport. Users authorize their own "
"Google account through the standard OAuth flow, so a calendar or another "
"Google feature uses that personal connection; an authorization keeps the "
"scopes granted before it. Requires a Google Cloud OAuth client whose "
"authorized redirect URIs list this database's callback."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_integration_microsoft
msgid ""
"Keeps each company's Microsoft Entra OAuth client in the credential vault "
"and calls Microsoft Graph through the integration transport. Users authorize"
" their own Microsoft account through the standard OAuth flow, so a calendar "
"or another Microsoft feature uses that personal connection. Requires a "
"Microsoft Entra app registration whose redirect URIs list this database's "
"callback; a single-tenant registration sets its tenant in the service's "
"authorization and token URLs."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_integration_twilio
msgid ""
"Keeps one Twilio account per company in the credential vault and sends every"
" Twilio API call through the integration transport. Sends SMS through the "
"account when the company selects Twilio as its SMS provider, records "
"delivery status from signed callbacks, and turns SMS received on the "
"company's Twilio numbers into one Discuss conversation per sender, whose "
"replies are sent back as SMS from the same number. Syncs the account's "
"numbers and their capabilities and can point a number's incoming-SMS webhook"
" at Odoo. Requires a Twilio Account SID and Auth Token, numbers able to send"
" and receive SMS, and a public HTTPS base URL for Twilio's webhooks."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_calendar_sync
msgid ""
"Keeps one synchronization account per user and provider: the delta token, "
"the stop flag and the last synchronization, beside the user's own connection"
" to the provider. Links each event and recurrence to its copy in each "
"account's calendar, and keeps a deleted one's link until its copy is "
"deleted. Runs every provider's synchronization from one scheduled action and"
" one route, answers the calendar view's status and its start, stop and pause"
" buttons for every installed provider, and lets a provider adapter (Google, "
"Outlook) supply only what is particular to it. Installs with the calendar "
"and integration modules; synchronizes nothing until an adapter is installed "
"and a user authorizes it."
msgstr ""

