msgid ""
"Supplies Austrian chart templates, company account defaults, tax groups and "
"a tax report containing U1/U30 sections. Adds balance-sheet and external-"
"code tags to configured liquidity accounts and uses the declared report-"
"layout dependencies. Requires applying the Austrian chart to the company; "
"electronic filing is not provided here."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_iot_payment_terminal
msgid ""
"Supplies a ctypes-based terminal driver base used by vendor-specific IoT "
"addons. Handles common transaction and device behavior but does not identify"
" or operate a terminal by itself. Requires a concrete terminal addon, its "
"native library and a supported host platform."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_purchase_tender_team
msgid ""
"Supplies access-control entries for purchase tenders when the purchasing "
"team integration is installed."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_sale_sms
msgid ""
"Supplies access-control entries for the SMS composer when Sales and SMS are "
"installed together."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_sale_tender_team
msgid ""
"Supplies access-control entries linking sales tender records with the sales-"
"team roles declared by its dependencies."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_iot_adam_scale
msgid ""
"Supplies an IoT handler that probes the supported serial protocol and reads "
"scale measurements and status. Requires compatible Adam Equipment hardware, "
"serial access and an operating IoT driver runtime. Install for the intended "
"scale configuration because serial probing can interact with other attached "
"devices."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_iot_ingenico
msgid ""
"Supplies an IoT payment-terminal driver and transaction message handling for"
" the implemented Ingenico protocol. Requires a compatible configured "
"terminal and working IoT connection. Point-of-sale usage also requires the "
"corresponding Ingenico POS integration and provider setup."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_html_editor
msgid ""
"Supplies an extensible HTML editor with frontend plugins, attachment and "
"media helpers, and view-editing support. Includes reusable HTML-field "
"history support. Available editing features depend on the plugins and "
"permissions enabled by the consuming application."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_esg_project
msgid ""
"Supplies an initiative project, task navigation and an ESG dashboard section"
" for its progress."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_theme_xiuman
msgid ""
"Supplies branded header and footer templates, colors, typography, page "
"layouts and catalog presentation assets for the Xiuman website. Includes "
"homepage, company, product and contact pages. Requires the website and shop "
"dependencies; website records and business catalog data are managed by "
"separate addons."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_room_gantt
msgid ""
"Supplies calendar-event Gantt views grouped by room for the room booking "
"integration."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_integration_github
msgid ""
"Supplies client helpers for repositories, branches, commits, webhooks, "
"issues, pull requests and reviews, plus a GraphQL query method. Seeds a "
"GitHub integration service and uses the shared transport and credential "
"records. Adds check run, commit status, workflow run, compare and branch "
"calls; mints GitHub App installation tokens limited to named repositories "
"from an app credential; and receives signed webhook deliveries that keep "
"pull requests and the checks of their head commit current, for other modules"
" to follow. Calling addons must provide credentials with permissions for the"
" requested GitHub operation."
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_purchase_mrp_workorder_quality
msgid ""
"Supplies demonstration records connecting purchasing, manufacturing work "
