#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_account_collection_payroll_loan
msgid ""
"When the treasury validates a remittance that hands in less than its "
"collector collected, the shortage, already charged to the collector, becomes"
" a draft employee loan on the company's configured payroll input type, split"
" into the configured number of payslips. Payroll reviews it, computes its "
"table and confirms it, which is the approval; until then nothing is "
"deducted. Reverting the remittance archives a loan that is not yet running "
"and is refused once it runs. The salary rule of that input type decides the "
"payroll entry; crediting the collector shortage account there settles the "
"charge."
msgstr ""

